label ch3_m_end:
    [   0] # RenpyUnlock: Unlock { UnlockType=Normal, UnlockName="the_lady_who_knows_everything", UnlockId=2266515947 }
    [   1] call showpoem(<compiled: CompiledExpression { instructions=[CompiledInstruction], constantFloats=[], constantStrings=["poem_m3"], constantObjects=[] }>)
    [   2] m 1a "You know..."
    [   3] m "I feel like learning and looking for answers are the sorts of things that give life meaning."
    [   4] m 1e "Not to get too philosophical or anything..."
    [   5] m 1a "But it was kind of on my mind, so that's what I wrote about."
    [   6] mc "I see..."
    [   7] mc "I never really put much thought into it."
    [   8] m 1d "In a way, it's almost paradoxical."
    [   9] m "Because if we had all the answers, wouldn't the world start to lose its meaning?"
    [  10] mc "You know, there's one thing I noticed..."
    [  11] mc "It seems like everyone in the club prefers writing about things that are more sad than happy."
    [  12] m 1k "Ahaha. Are you surprised?"
    [  13] m 1a "I mean, if everything was okay..."
    [  14] m "We wouldn't really have anything to write about, would we?"
    [  15] m "Humans aren't two-dimensional creatures."
    [  16] m "I think you'd know that better than anyone."
    [  17] mc "You mean one-dimensional...?"
    [  18] m 1l "Ah...yeah, that!"
    [  19] m 1a "Anyway..."
    [  20] m 3b "Here's Monika's Writing Tip of the Day!"
    [  21] m "Are you ever too shy to share your writing because you're afraid it's not that good?"
    [  22] m "It can be really disheartening to get a lukewarm response to something you put so much into."
    [  23] m "But if you find other people who enjoy writing, then sharing becomes a lot easier!"
    [  24] m "Because instead of just telling you that your writing is good, or okay, or bad..."
    [  25] m "They'll want to focus more on everything that went into it, and the things you can work on."
    [  26] m "It's much more encouraging that way, and it will make you want to continue improving."
    [  27] m "It's almost like having your own little Literature Club, don't you think?"
    [  28] m 3k "...That's my advice for today!"
    [  29] m "Thanks for listening~"
    [  30] return
